essage and the structure of the toolResult in toolResults.\n\nActually, I realize I need to look at what the recorded tap prompt is, to understand how the request was sent. The tap records show `n_messages`, `prompt_n`, `cache_n`, `predicted_n`. Let me focus on understanding:\n\n1. The agent_end messages list structure — roles and content\n2. How to match agent turns to tap records (by n_messages and order)\n3. The mem0 DB schema (memory_history, messages)\n4. The mem0 extraction prompt assembly\n\nLet me look at the full agent_end messages for a mem0 run to understand the message roles (user, assistant, system, toolResult, custom, etc.), and the memory DB schema.\n\nLet me also check the memory_history table schema and the messages table.\n\nLet me look at the mem0_extract_src.txt to understand how the mem prompt is assembled (generateAdditiveExtractionPrompt).\n\nLet me be efficient and look at several things. First, let me look at all the message roles in agent_end, and the memory DB schema. Let me run a comprehensive inspection.\n"}}
