{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a very clear picture of the data structures. Let me note the important ones:\n\n**event stream format:**\n- `session`: line 0, has type, version, id, timestamp, cwd\n- `agent_start`: type only\n- `turn_start`: type only\n- `message_start`: (need to check)\n- `message_end`: (need to check)\n- `message_update`: (streaming updates)\n- `tool_execution_start`: (need to check)\n- `tool_execution_end`: toolCallId, toolName, result (content is a list of {type, text}), isError\n- `turn_end`: message (full assistant message: role, content [thinking, toolCall...], api, provider, model, usage, stopReason, timestamp, responseId, responseModel, rawStopReason), toolResults (list of {role: toolResult, toolCallId, toolName, content})\n- `agent_end`: messages (full transcript: list of messages with role, content, sections...), event_type, timestamp\n\nKey: `agent_end` has the full `messages` list — the entire transcript including system prompt (with `sections` key) and all messages. This is what we use to reconstruct the transcript.\n\n**System prompt structure (from agent_end messages[0]):**\n- role: \"system\"\n- content: \"\" (empty string)\n- sections: {preamble, tools, rules, docs, addendum, project_context, skills, cwd, ...}\n\nSo the system message has `sections` dict and the actual system prompt is the concatenation of the section values. The PI_SECTION_ORDER from the old script was: [\"preamble\", \"tools\", \"rules\", \"docs\", \"addendum\", \"project_context\", \"skills\", \"cwd\"]. Let me verify what sections are actually present.\n\nLet me look at all the keys of sections in the system message, and check the message_start / message_end structure.\n\nLet me also look at the tool_calls in the message and the structure of the toolResult in toolResults.\n\nActually, I realize I need to look at what the recorded tap prompt is, to understand how the request was sent. The tap records show `n_messages`, `prompt_n`, `cache_n`, `predicted_n`. Let me focus on understanding:\n\n1. The agent_end messages list structure — roles and content\n2. How to match agent turns to tap records (by n_messages and order)\n3. The mem0 DB schema (memory_history, messages)\n4. The mem0 extraction prompt assembly\n\nLet me look at the full agent_end messages for a mem0 run to understand the message roles (user, assistant, system, toolResult, custom, etc.), and the memory DB schema.\n\nLet me also check the memory_history table schema and the messages table.\n\nLet me look at the mem0_extract_src.txt to understand how the mem prompt is assembled (generateAdditiveExtractionPrompt).\n\nLet me be efficient and look at several things. First, let me look at all the message roles in agent_end, and the memory DB schema. Let me run a comprehensive inspection.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The event stream is well-structured. The key is `agent_end` which carries the full `messages` transcript, and `turn_end` which carries per-turn data. Let me now understand the message roles in the transcript and the memory DB schema.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"cqQsc8ZKTYK3tQM4ok82xmooWUWWdojH","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/dev/garden && python3 -c \"\nimport json\nev=json.load(open('bench/results/2026-10-12/m1-ngram/recon/event_samples.json'))\nagent_end=ev['samples']['agent_end']['event']\nmsgs=agent_end['messages']\nprint('n messages in agent_end:', len(msgs))\nprint()\nprint('=== system message keys ===')\nprint([k for k in msgs[0].keys()])\nprint('sections keys:', list(msgs[0].get('sections', {}).keys()))\nprint()\nprint('=== all message roles ===')\nfor i,m in enumerate(msgs[:8]):\n    content_types=[]\n    c=m.get('content')\n    if isinstance(c,list):\n        content_types=[x.get('type') for x in c if isinstance(x,dict)]\n    print(f'msg {i}: role={m.get(\\\"role\\\")!r} | content_types={content_types}')\n    if m.get('role')=='system':\n        print('  (system has sections, content=%r)' % repr(m.get('content','')[:40]))\n\"","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"garden","model":"bonsai-agent","usage":{"input":1581,"output":1008,"cacheRead":30139,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":32728,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791836144361,"responseId":"chatcmpl-dpXuvpCjULS6xP2MxZBQE7O8C5YVfzpz","responseModel":"/home/josiah/models/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PQ2_0.gguf","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"cqQsc8ZKTYK3tQM4ok82xmooWUWWdojH","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"n messages in agent_end: 29\n\n=== system message keys ===\n['role', 'content', 'sections', 'timestamp', 'toolsAdded']\nsections keys: ['preamble', 'tools', 'rules', 'docs', 'cwd']\n\n=== all message roles ===\nmsg 0: role='system' | content_types=[]\n  (system has sections, content=\"''\")\nmsg 1: role='user' | content_types=['text']\nmsg 2: role='custom' | content_types=[]\nmsg 3: role='assistant' | content_types=['thinking', 'toolCall', 'toolCall']\nmsg 4: role='toolResult' | content_types=['text']\nmsg 5: role='toolResult' | content_types=['text']\nmsg 6: role='assistant' | content_types=['thinking', 'toolCall', 'toolCall']\nmsg 7: role='toolResult' | content_types=['text']\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791836169167}]}
